Issue: The parent node's repairs were all character-level: an affix trimmed off the end of an answer, or a one-edit slip snapped onto a memorised answer. A reply that reproduces a demonstrated answer with a whole stretch of it left out sits 2-3 characters away from that answer, so MAX_EDITS=1 never reached it and no memory-side path existed for it. The parent run's own failures are full of it: 19 of its 50 LawBench failures are replies whose charge set is a strict subset of the gold with no spurious charge at all, and in at least 7 of them (examples (7,0), (7,1), (8,1), (13,0), (13,1), (14,1), (36,0), (36,1), (46,0), (29,0)) the demonstrated answer was sitting in the memory with the dropped stretch inside it — "非法采伐、毁坏国家重点保护植物" answered as "非法采伐国家重点保护植物", "拐卖妇女、儿童" as "拐卖妇女", "窝藏、包庇" as "窝藏", "虚开增值税专用发票、用于骗取出口退税、抵扣税款发票" as "虚开增值税专用发票". The dropped material in every one of those cases is a stretch containing a character the memory demonstrates as an *internal* separator ("、" or ";"), which is exactly what separates an abbreviation of a demonstrated answer from a different answer: the reply "以危险方法危害公共安全" maps onto the demonstrated "过失以危险方法危害公共安全" by dropping "过失", but that stretch carries no demonstrated separator, so the two are different charges and the reply must stand.

Modification: solver/answer_space.py now reads one more thing off the frozen memory — what its answers look like *inside*. derive_answer_space reports "markers": the characters the memory shows sitting inside its demonstrated answers (punctuation present in at least two demonstrated answers, so a stray mark in a single answer demonstrates nothing). New restore_abbreviation() restores a reply to a demonstrated answer when: the reply is that answer with exactly one *contiguous* stretch left out, that stretch carries a demonstrated marker, the reply is not itself a demonstrated answer, and the shortest demonstrated answer the reply can be cut down to is unique (longer demonstrated answers that also contain the reply never win, which is what keeps "窝藏" from being restored to "危险驾驶;窝藏、包庇"). ground_answer applies it per answer component after the existing affix trim and one-edit snap. Missing memory, unparsable replies, prose and non-answers stay byte-identical.

